WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.800
Welcome back to the show!

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:07.740
We once again join SCP-682 and its&nbsp;
trusty macaw sidekick Jerry deep in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.180
the depths of the liminal abyss known&nbsp;
as The Backrooms. The hard-to-destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.020
reptile had been seemingly contained&nbsp;
within The Backrooms for such a lengthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:22.560
period of time that it was likely even the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation had given up on searching for it.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.020
After unintentionally no-clipping out&nbsp;
of reality, 682 was apparently doomed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.120
wander these endless labyrinthine realities&nbsp;
until the end of its miserable existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.800
The latest level that it had arrived in&nbsp;
appeared to take the form of vast desert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.440
stretching from horizon to horizon. Sandstorms&nbsp;
buffeted the creature, and powerful gusts of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.300
wind forced Jerry to take refuge: clinging&nbsp;
tightly to its much larger friend’s back.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.460
This was level 16, but there was far&nbsp;
more to it than first met the eye.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.120
As the lizard and bird made their&nbsp;
way across the titanic dunes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.520
strange lights began to circle in the&nbsp;
air above. These were entities known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.260
Light Guides - singularities of pale light&nbsp;
that bore a strong resemblance to “will o'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.360
the wisp” - ghostly fire elementals out of&nbsp;
folklore. Much like the mysterious wisps of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.760
legend, Light Guides appear to travelers in The&nbsp;
Backrooms whenever there is an impending danger.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.720
You’d think with all the malicious&nbsp;
entities and bizarre hazards that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.900
SCP-682 had encountered in the previous levels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.420
it would have seen a lot more of these - but&nbsp;
considering how dangerous 682 itself was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.940
the Light Guides probably had their nonexistent&nbsp;
hands full keeping other travelers away from it.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:41.280
Either way, their numbers and proximity meant&nbsp;
that whatever was about to happen was going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.620
be something perilous. Jerry squawked&nbsp;
and nibbled at SCP-682 with his beak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:51.420
trying to warn the reptile of the&nbsp;
danger. 682 had no idea what to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.220
expect but made sure to have its guard&nbsp;
up and keep its avian companion close.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.840
The creature’s instincts were sharp as&nbsp;
ever, and the second that the level began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:07.440
to rearrange itself, 682 was already taking&nbsp;
evasive action. The sand hardened and turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.600
to stone as great pyroclastic flows began&nbsp;
to erupt from what were once the dunes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:18.300
SCP-682 leaped across a deep fissure just as it&nbsp;
opened up beneath the lizard’s feet - narrowly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.040
avoiding a several hundred foot drop into&nbsp;
a lake of lava. Ash rained from the sky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.620
as all traces of the desert were completely&nbsp;
overwritten into this new volcanic landscape.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.320
This was the defining supernatural feature&nbsp;
of Level 16 - an environment that randomly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.600
reshaped itself into different geographical&nbsp;
climates and terrains. Now that it had seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:46.020
the level change completely once, SCP-682&nbsp;
was already over the concept. Rather than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.600
stick around and take a bath in the lava,&nbsp;
SCP-682 decided to follow the Light Guides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.620
towards what appeared to be a portal&nbsp;
made out of concentrated blue light.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.620
It passed through the portal&nbsp;
and found itself in a cramped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.800
hallway resembling those aboard a nautical vessel.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:08.220
Out with Level 16 and in with Level 17&nbsp;
- otherwise known as the naval aircraft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:13.980
carrier. Though there was no actual deck of the&nbsp;
proverbial carrier, nor any potential aircrafts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:18.660
in The Backrooms for it to transport. There&nbsp;
didn’t seem to be much happening on Level 17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:24.000
at least in comparison to the drastic&nbsp;
terrain shifting of Level 16. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.340
were also absolutely no entities to&nbsp;
be seen, as far as 682 could tell.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:35.460
Of course, Level 17 was vexing to the reptile in a&nbsp;
different way: the corridor it found itself in was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:41.640
such an extremely tight fit, and moving freely&nbsp;
was next to impossible. The Backrooms was once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.500
again telegraphing the fact that it was made&nbsp;
with humans and not overgrown lizards in mind.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:51.900
Waste of effort. 682 thought&nbsp;
to itself. Not even the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.200
disgusting human has enough&nbsp;
dumb luck to make it this far.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.140
After a few minutes of struggle, 682 shrunk&nbsp;
down to a more manageable size so it could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:06.780
traverse the hallways. It was now roughly the&nbsp;
size of a male hyacinth macaw - that is to say:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.460
Jerry-sized - and it crawled through the&nbsp;
narrow corridors of Level 17 with room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:16.860
to spare. There was still no sign of hostile&nbsp;
entities, and given the propensity for Clumps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.840
to come avalanching out of the woodwork&nbsp;
on previous levels, SCP-682 saw this as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:27.600
a mercy. It was also grateful to no longer&nbsp;
be exposed to the elements on Level 16.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:34.080
SCP-682 passed the time exploring the seemingly&nbsp;
empty corridors by having one-sided small talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:40.140
with Jerry. The macaw couldn’t do much more than&nbsp;
chirp and squawk back, and before too long 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:45.420
realized that it had very little to talk about.&nbsp;
Its main interests were slaughtering living things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:50.760
and breaching containment, and both of these&nbsp;
topics were irreverent to the current mood. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:55.800
wave of embarrassment washed over the creature, as&nbsp;
for the first time it had genuine concern that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:02.280
social interaction could go poorly. It didn’t want&nbsp;
to frighten Jerry away, or come across as awkward.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:07.680
It was just that conversation with like-minded&nbsp;
anomalies had been far easier at the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:13.140
since the shared experience of being contained&nbsp;
was always a good starting point. The reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:19.500
also had fond memories of the time it got to chat&nbsp;
with SCP-079 - an old A.I. that the foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:24.840
secured around the same time as itself.
 
Though it was an unusual feeling for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:30.780
creature so filled with contempt and hatred,&nbsp;
SCP-682 had started to realize that it wanted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:36.360
build the same kind of rapport with Jerry. Maybe&nbsp;
getting lost in The Backrooms was exactly the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:42.060
kind of life experience it needed to become more&nbsp;
approachable to the few beings it could respect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:48.540
That being said, the current level it was on was&nbsp;
rather underwhelming as a way of making memories.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:54.720
Just then, SCP-682 saw what appeared to be&nbsp;
an ordinary human up ahead. It had its back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.780
turned to the reptile and Jerry, and seemed to&nbsp;
be unaware of their presence. A sitting duck.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:07.980
Oh, good. A distraction. Thought the flustered&nbsp;
lizard. I was totally sounding like I had no life.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:14.280
SCP-682 charged towards the human as fast as its&nbsp;
shrunken body could carry it. Jerry followed suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.740
flapping his wings and flying alongside&nbsp;
682. As the duo approached, the human began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:25.140
to turn around. What 682 anticipated was a&nbsp;
look of abject horror on the human’s face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:31.260
but instead the entity simply stared through&nbsp;
682 as if the reptile wasn’t even there. 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:36.960
was confused, but even stranger was the fact&nbsp;
that its consciousness was starting to fade.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:43.140
682 blinked and in what felt like a second&nbsp;
later, it awoke at full-size, half-wedged in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:49.020
an aircraft carrier doorway. Jerry was squawking&nbsp;
up a storm, and that was presumably what had woken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:54.360
682 back up. It also seemed that making eye&nbsp;
contact with that humanoid entity had somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.360 --> 00:07:02.040
caused 682 to faint temporarily. The entity&nbsp;
itself was long gone: much to 682’s chagrin.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.180
This phenomenon was easy enough for any&nbsp;
expert in Backrooms lore to explain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:12.900
as Level 17 was home to unique entities known&nbsp;
as Imprints - which resembled humans but had the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.580
supernatural ability to induce brain death&nbsp;
in anything that looked them in the eyes.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:24.780
Even so, this was an unacceptable outcome to&nbsp;
SCP-682. Had the entities been growing stronger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:30.600
at the level number went higher or was the reptile&nbsp;
simply losing its mental fortitude? Maybe all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:35.400
strange properties of this place were compounding&nbsp;
on the creature and slowly making it go soft.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.780
682 shrunk down again and shook off&nbsp;
the shame of its encounter with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.860
imprint. The only way to prove that it was&nbsp;
better than The Backrooms was by advancing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.720
through all the levels and taking down&nbsp;
whatever entities stood in its way. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.980
would probably mean facing at least one more&nbsp;
pompous jerk with a spear - like Tiny and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:58.860
Argos before - and 682 relished the chance&nbsp;
to triumph in another bout of single combat.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:04.560
Besides, if another fair fight like those ones&nbsp;
were to take place, 682 would be able to show off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:10.080
how strong it was to Jerry. That alone was reason&nbsp;
enough to find the entrance to the next level.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:15.840
The time for brooding was over: it was&nbsp;
now time for action and adventure. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.940
if it took one hundred years, 682 would not&nbsp;
rest until it made it through every level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:26.640
of The Backrooms and left the entire hellish&nbsp;
dimension devoid of the life it so despised.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:31.920
It wandered the hallways of Level 17 until it&nbsp;
found a door that was discolored compared to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:37.440
other ones, almost as if there was a photonegative&nbsp;
spotlight shining on it from the other side. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.360
was about to pass through when the same imprint it&nbsp;
had encountered earlier stepped into the hallway.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:50.460
“Fool me once…” SCP-682 growled, and confidently&nbsp;
initiated a staring contest with the creature.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:56.100
That feeling of losing consciousness was felt&nbsp;
immediately, but this time 682 suppressed it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:00.840
through sheer will. With all of its vast&nbsp;
brainpower, it fought to stay awake and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:06.780
even began to concentrate the distressing emotions&nbsp;
into its gaze. The imprint stood and continued to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:12.180
look at 682, but within mere moments the entity&nbsp;
was frothing at the mouth and falling backwards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:17.460
against the wall - as if the effects of its own&nbsp;
stare were reflected back at it through a mirror.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.340
682 may have been caught off guard the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:25.440
but its signature adaptation abilities&nbsp;
meant that there was never a second time.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.720
Exit stage right.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.660
The reptile opened the door to the next level and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:35.400
moved on to Level 18 - which was&nbsp;
known as the level of memories.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:40.380
Level 18 was said to take on a subjective&nbsp;
appearance that was different to every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:45.720
individual wanderer but would usually resemble&nbsp;
a place from childhood. This was no different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:51.540
for SCP-682 - and the hard-to-destroy reptile was&nbsp;
shocked to find itself in the very same primeval&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:56.700
forest where it and its countless siblings&nbsp;
first went to war against ancient humankind.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.680
There were even corpses littered around&nbsp;
like in the futuristic hallways of level 15,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:07.440
only these dead creatures were far more familiar&nbsp;
to the reptile. The vast majority were human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:12.900
warriors in bronze-age armor, still gripping&nbsp;
antiquated weapons such as swords and axes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:18.720
Among these fallen humans were the occasional dead&nbsp;
giant beasts - though these bodies were rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:25.860
few in number as casualties on the SCP-682’s&nbsp;
side of this war had been almost nonexistent.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:30.720
682 had never thought it would see this&nbsp;
place or those of its kind that were too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:35.940
weak to survive the battlefield again.&nbsp;
It was a strange, uncomfortable feeling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:41.940
not helped by the raspy whispering voices&nbsp;
that seemed to linger in the wind of Level 18.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.360
Your father will never look for you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:52.140
for he has already transcended that momentary&nbsp;
flash of anger that brought you and the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:58.620
of your litter into being. He only has&nbsp;
further use for your mother, his bride.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:06.000
She is worth a million of you, no matter how many&nbsp;
battles you’ve fought in the name of his hate.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:12.120
Despite the ghoulish intensity of the whispering&nbsp;
voices, the words they said were clear and direct,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:18.420
impossible to mistake. But the part that&nbsp;
really caused SCP-682’s blood to boil was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:23.760
the fact that these voices seemed to know more&nbsp;
about its past than even The Foundation did.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:29.340
Tell me, disgraced Prince&nbsp;
of Wrath, what hurts more:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:33.960
the fact that you proved weak enough to&nbsp;
fall into the clutches of your greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:41.100
enemies or the fact that those same lab coats&nbsp;
and soldiers were the first ones that allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:48.000
you an identity of your own – distinct&nbsp;
from the whims of your pathetic father?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.080
Lost in the wicked siren&nbsp;
song of Level 18’s voices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:57.420
682 suddenly noticed that Jerry had flown&nbsp;
off again or perhaps he had never entered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:03.300
Level 18 with the reptile at all. It called&nbsp;
out for the macaw but there was no answer.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:09.240
SCP-682 found all of this to be very distressing,&nbsp;
especially since these whispers seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:14.760
come from some powerful unseen force that knew&nbsp;
exactly what the reptile viewed as its greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:19.920
failures. It was different from the influx of&nbsp;
negative thoughts that level 14 has caused,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:27.360
since that had been a product of 682 own minds.&nbsp;
What was happening here on level 18 was different.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:33.480
A separate, malevolent consciousness - perhaps&nbsp;
the creator of The Backrooms itself - was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:38.820
completely aware of all of 682’s childhood&nbsp;
trauma and was deliberately using it against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:43.920
the creature. Physical threats were one thing&nbsp;
that SCP-682 had always been able to overcome,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:49.560
but a psychological attack of this degree was&nbsp;
beyond the capabilities of even The Foundation.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:54.900
Still, there had to be a way out of Level&nbsp;
18 or at least a way back to Jerry. Either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:59.160
would have given 682 a bit of breathing&nbsp;
room from the influence of the whispers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:04.680
Fortunately, things weren’t quite as dire&nbsp;
as they seemed as SCP-682 was about to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.820
reminded that not all entities in&nbsp;
The Backrooms mean to do it harm.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:15.720
Enter Entity 198 - nicknamed the Plush Dino&nbsp;
by the explorer who first discovered it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:19.500
While Level 18 is not the only level&nbsp;
of The Backrooms it can appear on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:24.540
The Plush Dino often patrols the reality of&nbsp;
childhood memories in search of wanderers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:28.560
in distress. And in the compromised&nbsp;
psychological state it was in right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:36.240
SCP-682 surprisingly fit that description -&nbsp;
thus prompting Entity 198 to come to its aid.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:42.960
At first, SCP-682 didn’t know what to make of this&nbsp;
peculiar synthetic-looking entity. It approached&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.400
with no ill will and wordlessly attempted to&nbsp;
comfort the reptile through gentle contact.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:53.820
SCP-682 swiped at the creature with its claw.&nbsp;
As always, it was in no mood for cuddling with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:59.220
a stuffed toy. Entity 198 seemed able&nbsp;
to dodge the reptile’s attacks easily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:04.320
and continued to do so as SCP-682 made&nbsp;
repeated attempts to destroy it. Nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:08.820
connected, and the Plush Dino circled the&nbsp;
hard-to-destroy reptile without a scratch.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.820
“What do you want from me,&nbsp;
you worthless little creep!?”

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:17.280
682 screamed at the Dino, at which point the&nbsp;
entity turned and started to speed away in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:23.280
random direction. SCP-682 gave chase, pursuing&nbsp;
Entity 198 through its own childhood memories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:28.740
towards what appeared to be the door that had&nbsp;
led it into level 18 to begin with. The Plush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:33.360
Dino opened the door, got on the floor, and&nbsp;
proceeded to walk the dinosaur… into the door.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:37.500
Without even considering whether doing&nbsp;
so would send itself back to Level 17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:45.600
SCP-682 followed the plush dino and instead found&nbsp;
itself in The Backrooms Level 19 - The Attic.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:50.760
Turns out that being blinded by anger always&nbsp;
helps one get further in life! That’s a positive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:56.940
lesson with no unfortunate implications. Jerry&nbsp;
had already arrived in Level 19 prior to 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:02.640
so chasing the Plush Dino was even more of a smart&nbsp;
decision than the reptile could have imagined.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:07.020
“Jerry!” SCP-682 said, running up&nbsp;
to the macaw and wagging its tail.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:11.460
Jerry fluttered down from the attic&nbsp;
rafters and landed on 682’s snout.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:16.980
“Six-eight-two! Ahoy!” He squawked, having&nbsp;
remembered 682’s designation number.

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:23.040
Apparently, he had been paying attention to the&nbsp;
conversations earlier. This means that 682 had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:27.660
confirmation that it hadn’t totally screwed&nbsp;
up this new friendship yet. On top of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:31.920
it was nice to know that Jerry had no&nbsp;
intention of abandoning the reptile.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.740
This was certainly a warm and touching reunion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:38.760
though the continued presence of the&nbsp;
smugly grinning Plush Dino almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:44.280
ruined it. 682 snapped its head towards the&nbsp;
offending entity and barked an insult at it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:50.160
hoping that it would get the message and leave.&nbsp;
But Entity 198 did no such thing, preferring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:55.140
to silently watch the wholesome interaction&nbsp;
between 682 and Jerry from a safe distance.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.780
Whatever. SCP-682 thought.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:01.200
It wasn’t going to waste any more&nbsp;
time on the impish little stuffed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:05.040
animal. That’s when Jerry swooped down&nbsp;
and landed next to the Plush Dino.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.440
“One-Nine-Eight.” Jerry squawked.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:12.780
He then waddled across the wooden attic&nbsp;
floorboards in between 682 and 198 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:19.020
squawked again. It was as if he was trying to&nbsp;
introduce the two, and this mortified 682. Was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:24.840
this thing a friend of Jerry’s? And if so, did&nbsp;
that mean he was going to have to coexist with it?

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:29.220
At the very least, the Plush Dino didn’t&nbsp;
seem to be alive in the conventional sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:34.260
but whether that meant it was an animated&nbsp;
object or some kind of machine remained as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:38.940
vague and mysterious as most things in The&nbsp;
Backrooms. Even though it didn’t technically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:44.160
fall into the very broad category of “living&nbsp;
organism” that SCP-682 wanted to wipe out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:49.020
that didn’t automatically disqualify the&nbsp;
miniature monster as being disgusting.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:54.720
Especially if the dinosaur was getting overly&nbsp;
friendly with Jerry. The blue hyacinth macaw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.720 --> 00:17:01.560
belonged to 682 and it didn’t feel like sharing&nbsp;
- especially not with some clingy toy. After the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:07.860
awkward introductions were over, 682 and its two&nbsp;
tagalong companions had a look around at Level 19.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:12.420
It definitely resembled the attic of a&nbsp;
household, complete with dusty discarded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:17.760
furniture and several boxes of photo albums&nbsp;
and other mementos. There was also the orange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:25.020
glow - an unusual fiery light that emanated from&nbsp;
beneath the floorboards. SCP-682 didn’t know why,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:28.800
but the glow reminded it of the same&nbsp;
memories that it had just had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:33.720
relive on the previous level. This time&nbsp;
though, 682 was drawn to thinking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:38.760
the more positive aspects of its proverbial&nbsp;
childhood: if one could call crushing human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:43.620
skulls beneath its claws and facing down&nbsp;
entire armies of humans to be positives.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:48.600
The truth was that SCP-682 was being&nbsp;
mildly affected by the orange glow of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:53.760
Level 19 - which had the memetic ability to&nbsp;
insinuate its way into the formative memories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:59.040
of anyone who wandered through the level. But&nbsp;
682 had spent enough time having its childhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:02.340
ruined today, and decided to search for the exit.

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:07.140
After all, if there were no entities present on&nbsp;
this floor, it would be a waste of time to stick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:11.460
around and play into the hands of whatever&nbsp;
was making that orange glow. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:16.980
it seemed that entity 198 was already one&nbsp;
step ahead of SCP-682 in the hunt for an exit.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:22.260
The Plush Dino had located a severely damaged&nbsp;
wooden door with the number “20” painted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:28.020
orange on its surface. No doubt this was&nbsp;
the entrance to the next level. SCP-682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:31.440
was still very annoyed that the Plush&nbsp;
Dino had insisted on hanging around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:36.840
but if it was going to actually be useful, the&nbsp;
reptile would be sure to make the most of it.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:41.820
682, Jerry, and the Dino entered the&nbsp;
broken doorway, and found themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:46.140
inside of a wide open warehouse room.&nbsp;
There were several corridors leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:50.220
out of the room that appeared to be filled&nbsp;
with crates on wooden and plastic pallets. 
 &nbsp;

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:56.220
This was Level 20 - The Warehouse. Although it&nbsp;
resembled many earlier floors of the Backrooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:02.520
it was surprisingly finite. Both the corridors and&nbsp;
the room were not of an unusual size compared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:07.320
their equivalents in the real world, and according&nbsp;
to explorers, the warehouse itself was only about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:14.280
300 kilometers wide at the most. Those stats&nbsp;
weren’t especially impressive if you asked 682.

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:21.180
Whatever happened to the infinite labyrinths&nbsp;
of liminal spaces? SCP-682 wondered. Ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:26.160
since the city level it’s been nothing&nbsp;
but confined spaces, weird mindscrew ones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:31.560
and that landscape that kept changing for no&nbsp;
reason. What happened to the classic Backrooms?

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:36.300
SCP-682 quickly came to its senses&nbsp;
and realized what it was thinking.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.400
“Classic Backrooms?”

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:42.300
It sounded like one of those snobby&nbsp;
Foundation researchers deciding what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:48.840
was a genuine SCP and what wasn’t based on&nbsp;
some incredibly arbitrary standard. Besides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:53.940
there were no levels of the Backrooms that&nbsp;
were remotely acceptable for 682 - other than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:58.440
maybe level 9 - and breaking them down into&nbsp;
further categories went against the reptile's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:03.540
ultimate goal of destroying this horrendous&nbsp;
place and everything associated with it.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:07.740
It wouldn’t become like the Foundation&nbsp;
it hated by being specific and thorough.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:13.380
Broad sweeping statements were more SCP-682&nbsp;
style and when it came to The Backrooms:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.140
every level was equally disgusting.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:20.880
682 turned to its companions and growled&nbsp;
with what seemed to be excitement.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:25.560
“Jerry, let’s get moving. You&nbsp;
too, piece-of-garbage dinosaur.”

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:32.580
Now go check out “Could SCP-682 be Contained in&nbsp;
the Backrooms?” and “SCP-682 Slaughters Through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.960
the Backrooms” for more of our favorite&nbsp;
reptilian menace taking on the Backrooms!

